  partName: Rear Blade Shroud
  description: The Rear Blade Shroud is a thin, flat component located at the middle-rear
    center of the engine, crafted from Blades material. Similar to the Rear Blade
    Shroud and , it provides a protective casing for the Rear Blade , ensuring a
    smooth airflow and minimizing obstruction. Its identical design to the previous
    shrouds highlights the engine's use of standardized components, simplifying manufacturing
    and maintenance processes.
